girlfriend or  boyfriend or  or significant other you know they know  that they're going to get something but  what about  valentine's day for people who aren't  expecting a delivery at the door  so what he wanted to do was give roses  to people  that don't have their significant other  or a loved one in their life so he  prompted people by a social media to  nominate people to get a rose  and so he would go to these you know  these  residences where there were widows or  people who were having a really tough  time um  and and so this this became sort of you  know a a movement i guess  um and he was every year it was getting  bigger and bigger and bigger  and so when i talked to him he was such  a wonderful guy i love  chatting with him and he just had this  great sense of humor and  you know i asked him i'm like so you  have a girlfriend how does she feel  about this you know you going to give  roses to everybody and and he said well  you know she  she thinks it's great i said well of  course she does because you're doing  something important and his point was  i'm not giving roses to like you know  women  who i want to date i'm giving roses to  people who aren't expecting something  that they've had some kind of loss in  their life where they  they have lost somebody and maybe  they're not having a good day and just  a delivery of a rose can change their  you know their outlook and you can you  know  he sent me um notes that people wrote  afterwards about how important that one  gesture was  and then when i talked to seth he told  me something about himself he too  uh was diagnosed with diabetes and he  talked about his struggle  and how at one point he he got to the  point where he didn't want to live  anymore  and he told me this story and it just  you know it made my heart break  but the point was is that he was he's so  glad that he  wanted to stay alive and do this for  other people  and how it's important that when we go  through  challenges we realize that coming out of  those challenges we can be  better people we can do things to better  ourselves be better human beings  and so that just struck me because i  never thought about  him telling me this backstory to his  life but it was important because it  kind of gives you an  inside to where this guy is coming from  where his heart is and and you know his  background about how he  really truly wants to do good things for  other people to change their day  well janice i think your story is  basically proof that you're making your  own sunshine and  in a year that was was pretty bizarre um  you are welcome back anytime especially  if you want to talk about cuomo  and don't get and and don't get me  started on this newsome guy i'm i'm on  my own little  adventure with him so we're we're  definitely in this fight together  uh so i thank you i i hope i can see you  in long island sometime or you're always  welcome to come out here to la  megan knows my husband makes a pretty  pretty good chicken parm  can i tell you that i was so jealous  when she told me about her evening  there is no way she is going back to la  without  me and tow so that we can get together  you guys are always welcome to our home  uh and i thank you this was a wonderful  interview and and you know thank you for  your support and your kindness  and you my friend are also spreading  sunshine  there you go all right thanks a lot  welcome if you're looking for more  honest and thoughtful conversations  about politics instead of non-stop  yelling check out our politics playlist  and if you want to watch  full interviews on a variety of topics  watch our full episode playlist  all right over here and to get notified  of all future videos be sure to  subscribe and click the notification  bell
 

